    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dcf676c6_b4db2c77",
        "filename": "cmds/prezygote/prezygote.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-30T17:45:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since the goal is to remove everything, how about return 0 to keep it going?\n\nSecurity wise, an error case I can think of is when the attacker managed to change parent directory\u0027s  mode to non-writable, then unlink/rmdir would probably fail.  Or set some extended attributes.  We could have another pass of nftw if necessary, in order to recover from the error case.  WDYT?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 57,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 57,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "7f86363a3e784f8e99ace5c0ca222f705f743a37",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9b540080_ea13b48c",
        "filename": "cmds/prezygote/prezygote.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1249526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-30T20:25:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was thinking of that attack too. I\u0027m not sure how running it nftw again would change anything, we still wouldn\u0027t have permissions to remove it if we didn\u0027t the first time.\nLooking at all the the potential ways remove can fail: https://www.gnu.org/software/libc/manual/html_node/Deleting-Files.html, I don\u0027t see how any of them would be fixed by a second pass. The issue with returning 0 is that we aren\u0027t notified of any errors, which we would need if we wanted to prevent the user from booting a tampered image (if that\u0027s what we want to do).",
      "parentUuid": "dcf676c6_b4db2c77",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 57,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 57,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "7f86363a3e784f8e99ace5c0ca222f705f743a37",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "28920f56_eeca2325",
        "filename": "cmds/prezygote/prezygote.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-30T21:10:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, by the second pass, I meant the first pass to reset the mode/attributes to expected value.  Then we run this part.  I\u0027m not worried about the errors like EBUSY, since we are still in verified state (so we control every running things, thanks for dm-verity) and we just need to clean up data on disk before even using them (in theory we can reset everything).\n\nBut actually, since this process runs as root, unlink/rmdir would probably always success?  It\u0027d be nice to test with 1) some non-writable directory and file, and 2) immutable file (chattr +i filename).  I\u0027d feel comfortable with these two cases covered.",
      "parentUuid": "9b540080_ea13b48c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 57,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 57,
        "endChar": 13
      },
